<article class="help-article p-4">
    <header class="help-article-header mb-4">
        <span class="material-symbols-outlined help-article-icon">bolt</span>
        <h1 class="help-article-title">Fetch Indexes</h1>
        <p class="help-article-lead">
            Fetch indexes help describe how stored entities should be indexed for common fetch patterns.
        </p>
    </header>

    <h2 class="help-heading">Add an index</h2>
    <ol class="help-steps">
        <li><strong>Select an entity</strong> that already has attributes.</li>
        <li><strong>Open the main menu</strong> and choose <em>Add Fetch Index</em>.</li>
        <li><strong>Name the index</strong> and choose its collation type in the Inspector.</li>
        <li><strong>Add index elements</strong> in the center pane and choose the property or expression each element uses.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2 class="help-heading">Index elements</h2>
    <ul class="help-list">
        <li><strong>Property</strong> &mdash; choose one of the entity's attributes, or Expression for a calculated element.</li>
        <li><strong>Ascending</strong> &mdash; controls sort direction for the element.</li>
        <li><strong>Expression Result Type</strong> and <strong>Format</strong> &mdash; used when the element is an expression.</li>
        <li><strong>Partial Index Predicate</strong> &mdash; limits the rows included in the index.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="help-callout">
        <span class="material-symbols-outlined">speed</span>
        <div>
            <strong>Index for repeated queries.</strong>
            Add indexes for properties that appear often in fetch predicates, sorting, or uniqueness-like lookup flows.
        </div>
    </div>
</article>
